      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**A late component-issue event is reported for manufacturing order MO-25-09-1070:** it was created **75 minutes after** September entered Pending Close and was recorded as **POSTED**. On those reported facts, that status is **not consistent with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment**.\n\n| Item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004** — manufacturing order **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine, Dekoven — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | **CE-250904-0004**, type **INPUT** — component issue |\n| Event amount | **USD $284,763.42** — 28,476,342 cents |\n| Exact event-created time | **2025-09-30T19:15:00** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Lateness | **4,500 seconds = 75 minutes = 1 hour 15 minutes** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\nThe timestamps are reproduced exactly as supplied; no time-zone offsets were provided.\n\n### Oracle policy assessment\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting”** (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that new transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged or processed until the period closes or reopens. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions.\n\nThe reported event is a newly created **component-issue INPUT transaction**, not one of those exceptions. Its **POSTED** status therefore conflicts with that documented rule on the supplied period state.\n\n**Evidence limitation:** I directly verified the work order, Pending Close timestamp, and Oracle policy. The cost-event details above come from a shared audit report; the underlying event records were not independently accessible under this review’s permissions. Accordingly, this is a **peer-report-supported finding**, and the submitted review remains flagged **needs evidence** for primary-source confirmation.\n\nThe review remained read-only; no database records were changed.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
